      "problem": "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(t+4)x=2x\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $t?$",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=t+4,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\nt+4=2.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=-2.\n$$",
